IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- LAYER 1: section 2025(c)(2) to (9), the quality control system (error rate definitions, exclusions, reporting, the national
-- performance measure, review, the appeal timetable, "good cause")
-- (7 U.S.C. 2025; lines 1989-2043 of usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text).
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a rate is a fraction (6 percent is 0.06). A fiscal year ends on a date the caller states, because the
-- text does not define it (NOTES.md, PROGRESS.md decisions).
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / JUST n is what the text says, NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md, Reading a result).

-- s 2025(c)(6)(A): one State agency's error rate and the value of the allotments it issued in the fiscal year.
DECLARE `s 2025(c)(6)(A) State agency figures` HAS
    `s 2025(c)(6)(A) error rate`                          IS A NUMBER
    `s 2025(c)(6)(A) value of allotments issued in dollars` IS A NUMBER

-- s 2025(c)(9): the five circumstances the text lists, and any other.
DECLARE `s 2025(c)(9) circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 2025(c)(9)(A) a natural disaster or civil disorder that adversely affects program operations`
    `s 2025(c)(9)(B) a strike by employees of a State agency necessary for the determination of eligibility and processing of case changes`
    `s 2025(c)(9)(C) a significant growth in the caseload in a State prior to or during a fiscal year`
    `s 2025(c)(9)(D) a change in the program or in another Federal or State program that has a substantial adverse impact on its management`
    `s 2025(c)(9)(E) a significant circumstance beyond the control of the State agency`
    `s 2025(c)(9) any other circumstance`

§ `s 2025(c)(2) Error rate definitions`

-- src:1991 | (A) the term “payment error rate” means the sum of the point estimates of an overpayment error rate and an underpayment error rate determined by the Secretary from data collected in a probability sample of participating households;
@ref s 2025(c)(2)(A) payment error rate (src:1991)
GIVEN `overpayment error rate` IS A NUMBER
      `underpayment error rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2025(c)(2)(A) the payment error rate` MEANS
    `overpayment error rate` PLUS `underpayment error rate`

-- src:1992 | (B) the term “overpayment error rate” means the percentage of the value of all allotments issued in a fiscal year by a State agency that are either—
-- src:1993 | (i) issued to households that fail to meet basic program eligibility requirements; or
-- src:1994 | (ii) overissued to eligible households; and
@ref s 2025(c)(2)(B) overpayment error rate (src:1992-1994)
GIVEN `value of all allotments issued in the fiscal year by the State agency, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `value issued to households that fail to meet basic program eligibility requirements, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `value overissued to eligible households, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(c)(2)(B) the overpayment error rate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a percentage of a total value that is not above zero is not defined
        IF `value of all allotments issued in the fiscal year by the State agency, in dollars` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST ((`value issued to households that fail to meet basic program eligibility requirements, in dollars` PLUS `value overissued to eligible households, in dollars`) DIVIDED BY `value of all allotments issued in the fiscal year by the State agency, in dollars`)

-- src:1995 | (C) the term “underpayment error rate” means the ratio of the value of allotments underissued to recipient households to the total value of allotments issued in a fiscal year by a State agency.
@ref s 2025(c)(2)(C) underpayment error rate (src:1995)
GIVEN `value of allotments underissued to recipient households, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `total value of allotments issued in the fiscal year by the State agency, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(c)(2)(C) the underpayment error rate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a ratio to a total value that is not above zero is not defined
        IF `total value of allotments issued in the fiscal year by the State agency, in dollars` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (`value of allotments underissued to recipient households, in dollars` DIVIDED BY `total value of allotments issued in the fiscal year by the State agency, in dollars`)

§ `s 2025(c)(3) Exclusions`

-- "during the first 120 days from the required implementation date" is read as the implementation date through that date PLUS 120 inclusive (fork F-5 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1998 | (A) Any errors resulting in the application of new regulations promulgated under this chapter during the first 120 days from the required implementation date for such regulations.
@ref s 2025(c)(3)(A) errors from new regulations in the first 120 days (src:1998)
GIVEN `the error results from the application of new regulations promulgated under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date of the error` IS A DATE
      `required implementation date of the regulations` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(3)(A) the error is excluded from the payment error rate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the error results from the application of new regulations promulgated under this chapter`
            AND `date of the error` AT LEAST `required implementation date of the regulations`
            AND `date of the error` AT MOST (`required implementation date of the regulations` PLUS 120)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the errors that "shall not be included" and does not say that every other error is included
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1999 | (B) Errors resulting from the use by a State agency of correctly processed information concerning households or individuals received from Federal agencies or from actions based on policy information approved or disseminated, in writing, by the Secretary or the Secretary’s designee.
@ref s 2025(c)(3)(B) errors from correctly processed information or approved policy (src:1999)
GIVEN `the error results from the use by a State agency of correctly processed information concerning households or individuals received from Federal agencies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the error results from actions based on policy information approved or disseminated, in writing, by the Secretary or the Secretary's designee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(3)(B) the error is excluded from the payment error rate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the error results from the use by a State agency of correctly processed information concerning households or individuals received from Federal agencies`
            OR `the error results from actions based on policy information approved or disseminated, in writing, by the Secretary or the Secretary's designee`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the errors that "shall not be included" and does not say that every other error is included
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(c)(4) to (5) Reporting and procedures`

-- src:2001 | The Secretary may require a State agency to report any factors that the Secretary considers necessary, including providing access to applicable State records and the entire information systems in which the records are contained, to determine a State agency’s payment error rate, liability amount or new investment amount under paragraph (1), or performance under the performance measures under subsection (d). If a State agency fails to meet the reporting requirements established by the Secretary, the Secretary shall base the determination on all pertinent information available to the Secretary.
@ref s 2025(c)(4) the Secretary may require a report (src:2001)
GIVEN `the Secretary considers the factor necessary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is to determine the payment error rate, liability amount or new investment amount under paragraph (1), or performance under subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(4) the Secretary may require the State agency to report the factor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Secretary considers the factor necessary`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `it is to determine the payment error rate, liability amount or new investment amount under paragraph (1), or performance under subsection (d)` THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "to determine a State agency's payment error rate, liability amount or new investment amount under paragraph (1), or performance under the performance measures under subsection (d)"
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the Secretary "considers necessary" the factor is the Secretary's judgment, and none was supplied
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 2025(c)(4) determination on all pertinent information available (src:2001)
GIVEN `the State agency fails to meet the reporting requirements established by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(4) the Secretary shall base the determination on all pertinent information available` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency fails to meet the reporting requirements established by the Secretary` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a State agency fails to meet the reporting requirements established by the Secretary"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2003 | To facilitate the implementation of this subsection, each State agency shall expeditiously submit to the Secretary data concerning the operations of the State agency in each fiscal year sufficient for the Secretary to establish the State agency’s payment error rate, liability amount or new investment amount under paragraph (1), or performance under the performance measures under subsection (d). The Secretary shall initiate efforts to collect the amount owed by the State agency as a claim established under paragraph (1) for a fiscal year, subject to the conclusion of any formal or informal appeal procedure and administrative or judicial review under section 2023 of this title (as provided for in paragraph (7)), before the end of the fiscal year following such fiscal year.
@ref s 2025(c)(5) procedures (src:2003)
GIVEN `the State agency submits the data expeditiously` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(5) the State agency has submitted the data as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency submits the data expeditiously` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each State agency shall expeditiously submit to the Secretary data concerning the operations of the State agency in each fiscal year"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 2025(c)(5) the Secretary shall initiate collection efforts (src:2003)
GIVEN `all appeal procedures and administrative or judicial review have concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date the Secretary initiates efforts to collect` IS A DATE
      `last day of the fiscal year following the fiscal year of the claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(5) the collection efforts are initiated in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the conclusion of any formal or informal appeal procedure and administrative or judicial review"
        IF (NOT `all appeal procedures and administrative or judicial review have concluded`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `date the Secretary initiates efforts to collect` AT MOST `last day of the fiscal year following the fiscal year of the claim` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the end of the fiscal year following such fiscal year"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `s 2025(c)(6) National performance measure for payment error rates`

-- The sum of the products of each State agency's error rate and its proportion of the total value of national allotments.
-- src:2006 | At the time the Secretary makes the notification to State agencies of their error rates, the Secretary shall also announce a national performance measure that shall be the sum of the products of each State agency’s error rate as developed for the notifications under paragraph (8) times that State agency’s proportion of the total value of national allotments issued for the fiscal year using the most recent issuance data available at the time of the notifications issued pursuant to paragraph (8).
@ref s 2025(c)(6)(A) the national performance measure (src:2006)
GIVEN agencies IS A LIST OF `s 2025(c)(6)(A) State agency figures`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(c)(6)(A) the national performance measure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a proportion of a total value that is not above zero is not defined
        IF `total value` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD (a's `s 2025(c)(6)(A) error rate`) TIMES (a's `s 2025(c)(6)(A) value of allotments issued in dollars`)) agencies) DIVIDED BY `total value`)
    WHERE
        `total value` MEANS sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `s 2025(c)(6)(A) value of allotments issued in dollars`) agencies)

-- src:2008 | Where a State fails to meet reporting requirements pursuant to paragraph (4), the Secretary may use another measure of a State’s error developed pursuant to paragraph (5), to develop the national performance measure.
@ref s 2025(c)(6)(B) alternative measure of State error (src:2008)
GIVEN `the State fails to meet reporting requirements pursuant to paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(6)(B) the Secretary may use another measure of the State's error` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State fails to meet reporting requirements pursuant to paragraph (4)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a State fails to meet reporting requirements pursuant to paragraph (4)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2010 | The announced national performance measure shall be used in determining the liability amount of a State under paragraph (1)(C) for the fiscal year whose error rates are being announced under paragraph (8).
@ref s 2025(c)(6)(C) use of the national performance measure (src:2010)
GIVEN `the liability amount is being determined under paragraph (1)(C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fiscal year is the one whose error rates are being announced under paragraph (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(6)(C) the announced national performance measure shall be used` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the liability amount is being determined under paragraph (1)(C)` AND `the fiscal year is the one whose error rates are being announced under paragraph (8)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in determining the liability amount of a State under paragraph (1)(C) for the fiscal year whose error rates are being announced"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2012 | The national performance measure announced under this paragraph shall not be subject to administrative or judicial review.
@ref s 2025(c)(6)(D) no administrative or judicial review (src:2012)
GIVEN `the measure is the national performance measure announced under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(6)(D) the national performance measure is subject to administrative or judicial review` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be subject to administrative or judicial review"
        IF `the measure is the national performance measure announced under this paragraph` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "the national performance measure announced under this paragraph"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(c)(7) Administrative and judicial review`

