§ `s 2025(c)(8) Criteria for payment by a State agency`

-- src:2021 | (A) This paragraph applies to the determination of whether a payment is due by a State agency for a fiscal year under paragraph (1).
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(A) the paragraph applies (src:2021)
GIVEN `the determination is of whether a payment is due by a State agency for a fiscal year under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(8)(A) this paragraph applies to the determination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the determination is of whether a payment is due by a State agency for a fiscal year under paragraph (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies to the determination of whether a payment is due by a State agency for a fiscal year under paragraph (1)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2022 | (B) Not later than the first May 31 after the end of the fiscal year referred to in subparagraph (A), the case review and all arbitrations of State-Federal difference cases shall be completed.
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(B) the first May 31 after the end of the fiscal year (src:2022)
GIVEN `end of the fiscal year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2025(c)(8)(B) the first May 31 after the end of the fiscal year` MEANS
    IF Date 31 5 (DATE_YEAR `end of the fiscal year`) GREATER THAN `end of the fiscal year`
    THEN Date 31 5 (DATE_YEAR `end of the fiscal year`)
    ELSE Date 31 5 ((DATE_YEAR `end of the fiscal year`) PLUS 1)

@ref s 2025(c)(8)(B) the case review and arbitrations completed (src:2022)
GIVEN `end of the fiscal year` IS A DATE
      `date the case review and all arbitrations of State-Federal difference cases are completed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(8)(B) the case review and arbitrations are completed in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the case review and all arbitrations of State-Federal difference cases are completed` AT MOST (`s 2025(c)(8)(B) the first May 31 after the end of the fiscal year` `end of the fiscal year`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than the first May 31 after the end of the fiscal year"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2023 | (C) Not later than the first June 30 after the end of the fiscal year referred to in subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall—
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(C) the first June 30 after the end of the fiscal year (src:2023)
GIVEN `end of the fiscal year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2025(c)(8)(C) the first June 30 after the end of the fiscal year` MEANS
    IF Date 30 6 (DATE_YEAR `end of the fiscal year`) GREATER THAN `end of the fiscal year`
    THEN Date 30 6 (DATE_YEAR `end of the fiscal year`)
    ELSE Date 30 6 ((DATE_YEAR `end of the fiscal year`) PLUS 1)

-- src:2024 | (i) determine final error rates, the national average payment error rate, and the amounts of payment claimed against State agencies or liability amount established with respect to State agencies;
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(C)(i) final error rates determined (src:2024)
GIVEN `end of the fiscal year` IS A DATE
      `date the Secretary determines final error rates, the national average payment error rate and the amounts claimed or liability amounts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(8)(C)(i) the final error rates are determined in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the Secretary determines final error rates, the national average payment error rate and the amounts claimed or liability amounts` AT MOST (`s 2025(c)(8)(C) the first June 30 after the end of the fiscal year` `end of the fiscal year`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than the first June 30 after the end of the fiscal year referred to in subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall— (i) determine final error rates"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2025 | (ii) notify State agencies of the payment claims or liability amounts; and
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(C)(ii) State agencies notified (src:2025)
GIVEN `end of the fiscal year` IS A DATE
      `date the Secretary notifies State agencies of the payment claims or liability amounts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(8)(C)(ii) the State agencies are notified in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the Secretary notifies State agencies of the payment claims or liability amounts` AT MOST (`s 2025(c)(8)(C) the first June 30 after the end of the fiscal year` `end of the fiscal year`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than the first June 30 after the end of the fiscal year referred to in subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall— (i) determine final error rates, the national average payment error rate, and the amounts of payment claimed against State agencies or liability amount established with respect to State agencies; (ii) notify State agencies of the payment claims or liability amounts"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2026 | (iii) provide a copy of the document providing notification under clause (ii) to the chief executive officer and the legislature of the State.
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(C)(iii) copy to the chief executive officer and the legislature (src:2026)
