        IF `date the Secretary provides the copy` AT MOST (`s 2025(c)(8)(C) the first June 30 after the end of the fiscal year` `end of the fiscal year`)
            AND `it goes to the chief executive officer of the State`
            AND `it goes to the legislature of the State`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide a copy of the document providing notification under clause (ii) to the chief executive officer and the legislature of the State"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- The deadline in (D), (E), (F) or (G), extended by the administrative law judge for cause shown (subparagraph (I)): the later of the two.
-- src:2036 | (I) The deadlines in subparagraphs (D), (E), (F), and (G) shall be extended by the administrative law judge for cause shown.
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(I) deadlines extended for cause shown (src:2036)
GIVEN `the deadline in subparagraph (D), (E), (F) or (G)` IS A DATE
      `the extended deadline the administrative law judge allows for cause shown` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2025(c)(8)(I) the deadline as extended for cause shown` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the extended deadline the administrative law judge allows for cause shown`
    WHEN JUST extended THEN
        IF extended GREATER THAN `the deadline in subparagraph (D), (E), (F) or (G)`
        THEN extended
        ELSE `the deadline in subparagraph (D), (E), (F) or (G)`
    OTHERWISE `the deadline in subparagraph (D), (E), (F) or (G)`

@ref s 2025(c)(8)(I) shall be extended for cause shown (src:2036)
GIVEN `cause is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(8)(I) the administrative law judge shall extend the deadline` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `cause is shown` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for cause shown"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2028 | (i) a notice of appeal, not later than 10 days after receiving a notice of the claim or liability amount; and
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(D)(i) notice of appeal within 10 days (src:2028)
GIVEN `date the State agency received the notice of the claim or liability amount` IS A DATE
      `date the State agency submitted the notice of appeal to the administrative law judge` IS A DATE
      `the extended deadline the administrative law judge allows for cause shown` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(8)(D)(i) the notice of appeal is submitted in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the State agency submitted the notice of appeal to the administrative law judge` AT MOST (`s 2025(c)(8)(I) the deadline as extended for cause shown` (`date the State agency received the notice of the claim or liability amount` PLUS 10) `the extended deadline the administrative law judge allows for cause shown`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a notice of appeal, not later than 10 days after receiving a notice of the claim or liability amount"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2029 | (ii) evidence in support of the appeal of the State agency, not later than 60 days after receiving a notice of the claim or liability amount.
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(D)(ii) evidence within 60 days (src:2029)
