      `date the State agency submitted evidence in support of the appeal` IS A DATE
      `the extended deadline the administrative law judge allows for cause shown` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(8)(D)(ii) the evidence in support of the appeal is submitted in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `date the State agency submitted evidence in support of the appeal` AT MOST (`s 2025(c)(8)(I) the deadline as extended for cause shown` (`date the State agency received the notice of the claim or liability amount` PLUS 60) `the extended deadline the administrative law judge allows for cause shown`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "evidence in support of the appeal of the State agency, not later than 60 days after receiving a notice of the claim or liability amount"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2030 | (E) Not later than 60 days after a State agency submits evidence in support of the appeal, the Secretary shall submit responsive evidence to the administrative law judge to the extent such evidence exists.
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(E) responsive evidence within 60 days (src:2030)
GIVEN `such evidence exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date the State agency submitted evidence in support of the appeal` IS A DATE
      `date the Secretary submitted responsive evidence` IS A DATE
      `the extended deadline the administrative law judge allows for cause shown` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(8)(E) the responsive evidence is submitted in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent such evidence exists"
        IF (NOT `such evidence exists`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `date the Secretary submitted responsive evidence` AT MOST (`s 2025(c)(8)(I) the deadline as extended for cause shown` (`date the State agency submitted evidence in support of the appeal` PLUS 60) `the extended deadline the administrative law judge allows for cause shown`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 60 days after a State agency submits evidence in support of the appeal, the Secretary shall submit responsive evidence"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2031 | (F) Not later than 30 days after the Secretary submits responsive evidence, the State agency shall submit rebuttal evidence to the administrative law judge to the extent such evidence exists.
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(F) rebuttal evidence within 30 days (src:2031)
GIVEN `such evidence exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date the Secretary submitted responsive evidence` IS A DATE
      `date the State agency submitted rebuttal evidence` IS A DATE
      `the extended deadline the administrative law judge allows for cause shown` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(8)(F) the rebuttal evidence is submitted in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent such evidence exists"
        IF (NOT `such evidence exists`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `date the State agency submitted rebuttal evidence` AT MOST (`s 2025(c)(8)(I) the deadline as extended for cause shown` (`date the Secretary submitted responsive evidence` PLUS 30) `the extended deadline the administrative law judge allows for cause shown`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 30 days after the Secretary submits responsive evidence, the State agency shall submit rebuttal evidence"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2033 | (i) not later than 60 days after receipt of rebuttal evidence submitted by the State agency; or
-- src:2034 | (ii) if the State agency does not submit rebuttal evidence, not later than 90 days after the State agency submits the notice of appeal and evidence in support of the appeal.
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(G)(i)-(ii) decision within 60 days of rebuttal or 90 days of the notice and evidence (src:2033-2034)
GIVEN `date the administrative law judge received rebuttal evidence` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date the State agency had submitted both the notice of appeal and evidence in support` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2025(c)(8)(G) the last day for the administrative law judge's decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date the administrative law judge received rebuttal evidence`
    WHEN JUST received THEN received PLUS 60
    OTHERWISE `date the State agency had submitted both the notice of appeal and evidence in support` PLUS 90

-- src:2032 | (G) The administrative law judge, after an evidentiary hearing, shall decide the appeal—
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(G) after an evidentiary hearing the judge shall decide (src:2032)
GIVEN `the administrative law judge held an evidentiary hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date the administrative law judge received rebuttal evidence` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date the State agency had submitted both the notice of appeal and evidence in support` IS A DATE
      `date the administrative law judge decided the appeal` IS A DATE
      `the extended deadline the administrative law judge allows for cause shown` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(8)(G) the appeal is decided in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after an evidentiary hearing, shall decide the appeal"
        IF (NOT `the administrative law judge held an evidentiary hearing`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `date the administrative law judge decided the appeal` AT MOST (`s 2025(c)(8)(I) the deadline as extended for cause shown` (`s 2025(c)(8)(G) the last day for the administrative law judge's decision` `date the administrative law judge received rebuttal evidence` `date the State agency had submitted both the notice of appeal and evidence in support`) `the extended deadline the administrative law judge allows for cause shown`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall decide the appeal— (i) not later than 60 days after receipt of rebuttal evidence submitted by the State agency; or (ii) if the State agency does not submit rebuttal evidence, not later than 90 days"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2035 | (H) In considering a claim or liability amount under this paragraph, the administrative law judge shall consider all grounds for denying the claim or liability amount, in whole or in part, including the contention of a State agency that the claim or liability amount should be waived, in whole or in part, for good cause.
@ref s 2025(c)(8)(H) all grounds, including waiver for good cause (src:2035)
GIVEN `the administrative law judge considered all grounds for denying the claim or liability amount, in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency contends that the claim or liability amount should be waived for good cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the administrative law judge considered that contention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(8)(H) the administrative law judge has considered what the text requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the administrative law judge considered all grounds for denying the claim or liability amount, in whole or in part`
            AND ((NOT `the State agency contends that the claim or liability amount should be waived for good cause`) OR `the administrative law judge considered that contention`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the administrative law judge shall consider all grounds for denying the claim or liability amount, in whole or in part, including the contention of a State agency that the claim or liability amount should be waived"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `s 2025(c)(9) Good cause defined`

-- src:2038 | As used in this subsection, the term “good cause” includes—
-- src:2039 | (A) a natural disaster or civil disorder that adversely affects supplemental nutrition assistance program operations;
-- src:2040 | (B) a strike by employees of a State agency who are necessary for the determination of eligibility and processing of case changes under the supplemental nutrition assistance program;
-- src:2041 | (C) a significant growth in the caseload under the supplemental nutrition assistance program in a State prior to or during a fiscal year, such as a 15 percent growth in caseload;
-- src:2042 | (D) a change in the supplemental nutrition assistance program or other Federal or State program that has a substantial adverse impact on the management of the supplemental nutrition assistance program of a State; and
-- src:2043 | (E) a significant circumstance beyond the control of the State agency.
@ref s 2025(c)(9)(A)-(E) good cause (src:2038-2043)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 2025(c)(9) circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(9) the circumstance is good cause` MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the term good cause includes" the five listed; a circumstance not listed is not said to be excluded
    WHEN `s 2025(c)(9) any other circumstance` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2041 | (C) a significant growth in the caseload under the supplemental nutrition assistance program in a State prior to or during a fiscal year, such as a 15 percent growth in caseload;
@ref s 2025(c)(9)(C) a significant growth in the caseload, such as 15 percent (src:2041)
GIVEN `growth in the caseload` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(c)(9)(C) the growth in the caseload is a significant growth` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `growth in the caseload` AT LEAST 0.15 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "such as a 15 percent growth in caseload" is an example, not a threshold
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
